5 CONCLUSION
In this work we present ORC-MANL, a theoretically justified and empirically validated approach for nearest neighbor graph pruning. We rigorously demonstrate that shortcut edges necessarily exhibit particularly negative ORC for graphs sampled from manifolds with a bounded level of isotropic noise. Our method also validates the removal of any edge by using a theoretically derived bound on graph distances implied by the geometry of shortcut edges. We qualitatively and quantitatively demonstrate that ORC-MANL is beneficial to a variety of downstream geometric data analysis tasks on synthetic and real data. We also compare our method to baselines from the literature in its ability to correctly prune shortcut edges and avoid non-shortcut edges.
